cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  AI Overview Cited-Domains Study: which domains Google's AI Overview cites on
  24 buyer searches
message: If you use this dataset, please cite it.
type: dataset
authors:
  - given-names: Minel
    family-names: Gunesoglu
    affiliation: Is My Brand in AI
    email: minel@ismybrandinai.com
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0009-0009-4823-6016'
abstract: >-
  Twenty-four "best [category]" buyer searches across business software,
  consumer products, finance and lifestyle were run once each through Google on
  10 June 2026, with US English settings, and every domain listed in
  the AI Overview source panel was recorded by hand. Twenty-one searches
  produced an AI Overview; three physical retail searches returned a Shopping
  grid instead. Reddit was cited in 13 of the 21 AI Overviews, more than twice
  the next domains, Forbes and YouTube at 6 each, followed by PCMag (5), Zapier
  (4) and NerdWallet (3). A forum, Reddit or the Clark Howard community, was
  cited in 14 of the 21. An AI Overview listed a median of 8 sources, range 5
  to 12. The per-query rows and a script that recounts every published figure
  from them are included.
keywords:
  - Google AI Overviews
  - AI search
  - citation
  - generative engine optimization
  - Reddit
  - search engine results page
